+## Routes
+
+The complete route list is in `README.md`.
+
+- `POST /import/sales`: accepts `{ "csv": "ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty\n..." }`.
+  Columns may be reordered. CSV uses the same quoted-field format as item
+  imports (no embedded newlines). `soldAt` must include a time and timezone;
+  `qty` is positive with at most 3 decimal places. Returns
+  `{ "tickets": 2, "dishes": 5 }`, counting new tickets and summed dish quantities.
+  Previously imported tickets are skipped. All rows are validated; errors
+  identify the CSV row (header is row 1) and leave the whole file unimported.
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD`: returns an array of
+  `{ "itemId": 1, "theoretical": 2, "actual": 3, "difference": 1 }`, sorted by
+  item id, for items with either quantity above zero. Days are inclusive UTC
+  days; `from` must not follow `to`. Theoretical use is the ingredient snapshot
+  of sales sold in the period. Actual use includes every consume movement in
+  the period. Difference is actual minus theoretical, rounded to 3 decimals.
