+## Sales (schema 3)
+
+Schema 2 files migrate by adding `sales: []` and `seq.sale`. Sales have an
+integer `id`, a `ticket` string, normalized UTC `soldAt`, `dishId`, positive
+`qty` (up to 3 decimal places), and `ingredients` containing the scaled
+`itemId`/`qty` quantities at import time. Recipe edits do not change history.
+All rows for a new ticket in one file are imported together; tickets present
+before that import are skipped. A failed file changes neither stock, sales,
+ledger nor sequences. Sales consumption movements use the sale instant and
+`ref: sale:<ticket>`. Variance is actual minus theoretical, rounded to 3 decimals.
